                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Lords of Football is basically The Sims with a football team bolted on, and I spent most of my time babysitting players instead of coaching them. Half my squad ended up hooked on gambling or booze, and dragging them to the clinic was honestly the funniest part of the game. The problem is the loop of training, nightlife and match day gets repetitive fast, and the matches drag because the AI is so dumb you have to spam commands just to score. You can't buy players either, you hand the chairman a wishlist and hope he delivers. Add the memory crashes that make you save after every match, and I can't recommend it unless it's on a deep sale and you're curious about the concept.",
